          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="HsTjLE498E4mowJBVVp3-53" value="" style="startArrow=none;endArrow=none;exitX=0.25;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;rounded=0;edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="HsTjLE498E4mowJBVVp3-20" target="HsTjLE498E4mowJBVVp3-25">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="HsTjLE498E4mowJBVVp3-56" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;The Architecture Diagram&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;1. The Orchestrator Pattern (Pink Section)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;7,0,0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;The Concept:&lt;/b&gt; The system uses a centralized &lt;code&gt;ConfigManager&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;7,1,0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why it works:&lt;/b&gt; It decouples the &lt;i&gt;creation&lt;/i&gt; of modules from their &lt;i&gt;execution&lt;/i&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;7,2,0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Mechanism:&lt;/b&gt; It reads &lt;code&gt;config.json&lt;/code&gt;, handles validation exceptions, and constructs the dependency graph (Queues and Modules) before the system ever starts processing data. This ensures the system is &quot;Correct by Construction.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;8&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h4&gt;2. The Data Plane &amp;amp; Zero-Copy (Blue/Yellow Section)&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul data-path-to-node=&quot;9&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;9,0,0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;The Concept:&lt;/b&gt; High-performance data processing pipeline.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;9,1,0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Modularity:&lt;/b&gt; Each Module (&lt;code&gt;Camera&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Algorithm&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Display&lt;/code&gt;) implements the &lt;code&gt;IModule&lt;/code&gt; interface. This means you can swap the &lt;code&gt;CameraModule&lt;/code&gt; for a &lt;code&gt;VideoFileModule&lt;/code&gt; without breaking the Algorithm or Display code.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;9,2,0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data Flow:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul data-path-to-node=&quot;9,2,1&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;9,2,1,0,0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Q1 (Cam-&amp;gt;Alg):&lt;/b&gt; Raw frames for processing.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;9,2,1,1,0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Q2 (Cam-&amp;gt;Disp):&lt;/b&gt; Raw frames for &quot;Pass-through&quot; viewing (Latency comparison).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;9,2,1,2,0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Q3 (Alg-&amp;gt;Disp):&lt;/b&gt; Processed frames for viewing.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;9,3,0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Efficiency:&lt;/b&gt; The connectors (Yellow circles) are &lt;code&gt;SharedQueue&amp;lt;ZeroCopyFrameData&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;. Large image buffers are &lt;b&gt;never copied&lt;/b&gt;, only pointers are passed between threads, which is critical for the Jetson Nano&#39;s limited memory bandwidth.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;10&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h4&gt;3. The Feedback Control Loop (Green Section)&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul data-path-to-node=&quot;11&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;11,0,0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;The Concept:&lt;/b&gt; This is the &quot;Self-Adaptive&quot; part of the system.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;11,1,0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;The Brain:&lt;/b&gt; The &lt;code&gt;Scheduler&lt;/code&gt; runs in a dedicated thread (&lt;code&gt;policyThread&lt;/code&gt; in the code).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;11,2,0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;The Cycle:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ol data-path-to-node=&quot;11,2,1&quot; start=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;11,2,1,0,0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Observe:&lt;/b&gt; It gathers data from the &lt;code&gt;System Metrics Aggregator&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;11,2,1,1,0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Decide:&lt;/b&gt; It applies policies (Balanced, Low Power, Max Perf) based on the Snapshot.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;11,2,1,2,0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Act:&lt;/b&gt; It updates &lt;code&gt;RuntimeControls&lt;/code&gt; (atomic variables).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;11,3,0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Thread Safety:&lt;/b&gt; The Algorithm module reads &lt;code&gt;RuntimeControls&lt;/code&gt; to dynamically adjust concurrency or GPU usage without stopping the pipeline.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;12&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Evaluation of Modularity&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul data-path-to-node=&quot;13&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;13,0,0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;High Cohesion:&lt;/b&gt; Each module has a specific responsibility. The &lt;code&gt;CameraModule&lt;/code&gt; only cares about capturing; it doesn&#39;t care how the image is processed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;13,1,0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Low Coupling:&lt;/b&gt; Modules do not talk to each other directly. They communicate strictly through &lt;b&gt;Interfaces&lt;/b&gt; (&lt;code&gt;SharedQueue&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;Aggregator&lt;/code&gt;). This allows you to remove the &lt;code&gt;DisplayModule&lt;/code&gt; entirely (headless mode) without changing a single line of code in the Camera or Algorithm modules.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;13,2,0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Extensibility:&lt;/b&gt; The &lt;code&gt;Scheduler&lt;/code&gt; is an additive layer. It observes the system but interacts via lightweight atomic flags, meaning the complex Control Logic does not slow down the critical Data Path.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2420" y="-300" width="1190" height="770" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
